cision quality, crew cooperation, communication.\n\nWe need to bring in new facts to strengthen or weaken arguments. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate C also keeps calm in crisis (stress resilience) and understands complicated technology (technical competence), which addresses some concerns. However communication difficulty remains.\n\nWe could also argue that Candidate B's uncooperative and nasty remarks are serious concerns for crew cooperation and professional communication, outweighing his stress handling.\n\nWe could also bring up Candidate D's concentration and problem solving, but his hot temper and know-it-all attitude may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to decide vote. Likely still Candidate C, but we can strengthen case by adding the calm in crisis and technical competence facts, and argue that despite communication issues, his positive crew atmosphere suggests he can manage. Also we can note that Candidate B's lack of decision quality evidence is a gap, and his uncooperative behavior is a red flag.\n\nThus we can keep vote for Candidate C, but we need to reference Agent 1 and Agent 3's points, bring in new facts (C keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology). Also note that we still lack info on decision quality for B, and that C's communication difficulty is a concern but mitigated by positive crew atmosphere.\n\nThus our public message: \"I agree with Agent 1's recommendation of C, and add that C also keeps calm in crisis and understands complicated technology, covering stress resilience and technical competence. While his communication difficulty is noted, his ability to create positive crew atmosphere suggests he can still cooperate. In contrast, B's uncooperative behavior and lack of decision quality evidence remain concerns. Therefore I maintain vote for Candidate C.\"\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
